From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] whyred: accept fixed 512-byte geometry negotiation

XNU spec_open selects a 512-byte block size and restores the reported size
even when bdevvp opens the disk with FREAD. Returning ENOTTY for the restore
causes ENXIO and the bdevvp failed: open panic before APFS is mounted.

Accept only the already active 512-byte size. This ioctl changes no hardware
registers or media, and FWRITE opens and write strategy requests remain denied.

--- a/bsd/dev/whyred_emmc_pio_probe.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/whyred_emmc_pio_probe.c
@@ -1022,6 +1022,9 @@
 	case DKIOCGETPHYSICALBLOCKSIZE:
 		*v32 = WHYRED_GPT_BLOCK_BYTES;
 		return 0;
+	case DKIOCSETBLOCKSIZE:
+		/* spec_open selects and restores 512-byte sectors, even for FREAD. */
+		return *v32 == WHYRED_GPT_BLOCK_BYTES ? 0 : EINVAL;
 	case DKIOCGETBLOCKCOUNT:
 		if (part == NULL) return ENXIO;
 		*v64 = part->last - part->first + 1;
